==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Vodka Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Royal Guard Cat''' when obtained from [[Requiem for Angels (Merciless)]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
At first glance, Cossack Cat's impressive spammable DPS is promising, but his range cripples him. He can only outrange 3 Relic enemies, which are [[Relic Doge]], [[Oldhorn]] and [[Sir Rel]]. Against Sir Rel, he performs terribly because of his single-target attack, considering that in almost all their appearances, Sir Rels are spawned in groups or are supported by multiple other peons. Relic Doge behaves similarly, although he isn't as threatening as Sir Rel. He performs well against single Oldhorns, but when there are multiple of them, notably in [[Supervolcano]], he gets easily overwhelmed by them and performs worse than area DPS units such as [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Flying Cat]] would do against them. There are very few situations where this Cat is useful, and he gets outclassed by [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapsticks]] easily.

==='''True Form'''===
Royal Guard Cat notably gains Alien target and higher DPS, with 5.3k at Level 30. This totals to 21.2k DPS and 15.9k DPS against Aliens and Relics respectively, which is rather impressive despite his range, tearing through melee threats such as [[Nimoy Bore]], [[Cyberhorn]], [[Mesocosmocyclone]] and [[Star Peng]], and can potentially sneak a few hits into [[Cli-One]] and even [[Ursamajor]]. With his lower price and higher DPS for the cost, he can be better for lone aliens such as the ones mentioned above, sometimes making him a better candidate than [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]], although Chill Cat is preferable if there are aliens he cannot outrange, such as [[General GreGory]] and if there are too many aliens for Royal Guard to handle. Do note that he has lower range than [[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Jetpack Cat]] meaning that if he goes in front first, he'll get hit before Jetpack does. Thanks to his health increase, his Relic targetting allows him to easily rush hits onto [[Othom]] and [[Lowkey]], especially if supported by other units like [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] and [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] who can weaken and freeze them for a brief amount of time respectively, though for many other matchups Slapstick Cats are preferred for their better range and Area Attack. His Single Attack won't allow him to deal with swarms of peons, so beware. He has even better value in {{4c}} restriction stages, where superior alternatives are not available and especially 4-crown [[Revival of Origin]] and more so in the [[Revival of Origin/Invasion|Invasion]] stage.

The last buff he gains is immunity to [[Wave Attack]]. This is fairly useful for him to not die to stray waves set off by other enemies and wavers within his traits such as [[Haniwanwan]] and [[Elizabeth the LVIth]], and he can get several hits onto [[Youcan]] thanks to its long attack cycle, though be warned he cannot outrange [[Masked Grandmaster Cat (Enemy)|Masked Grandmaster Cat]] and [[Gigahaniwan]] reliably, being shredded easily by their attacks or support. While his low range allows him to serve as a Wave Immune meatshield, far superior alternatives already exist.

Overall, while his True Form may not seem like much at a first glance, it is amazing enough to give it a usable and better niche at what it tried to do previously.

